caption: Species Types
species-rule: species-types

Every Species is one of three types. A character normally has one Natural Species and may also possess Physical Modification or Supernatural Modification Species that overlay it.

Ascension Species is not a fourth Species type. It is a Domain-level acquisition and reward category: a Character Species gained through that Domain's explicitly defined ascension process. Every Ascension Species must still identify itself as Natural, Physical Modification, or Supernatural Modification. A Natural Ascension Species replaces the prior Natural Species; a Modification Ascension Species overlays it and follows the normal compatibility rules for Modification Species. Universal eligibility, Ascension Work, actual-sheet-delta Template Cost, Ascension Debt, failure, adulthood, and cross-Ascension rules are defined in Ascension Mechanics in the Domains folder.

Natural Species is the Species into which a being is born. Changing it normally requires sufficiently advanced retroviral engineering or permanent species-changing magic, such as Tier 2 Greater Wish or any permanent Tier 3 alteration.

Physical Modification Species alter physiology without replacing the Natural Species. Becoming a ghost is a Physical Modification: the character is dead and follows the ghost rules in Godmath. Liches and other primarily bodily undead templates are also Physical Modifications.

Supernatural Modification Species alter the soul and mind, with bodily changes occurring as a secondary effect. Ascended, the Tier 2 acquired template from Psychic Magic, is a Supernatural Modification laid over the Natural Species. Lycanthropy and Vampirism are also Supernatural Modifications.

Cybernetics are not a Species change. Uplifts are distinct Natural Species, and Changelings are their own Species.
